cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ChromoSort in published work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ChromoSort"
abstract: >-
  ChromoSort is a reference-guided genome assembly curation toolkit for sorting
  contigs, conservatively cleaning mostly-correct assemblies, splitting reviewed
  chimeric contigs, making manual cuts, reviewing dot plots, scaffolding final
  ordered contigs, and applying reviewed graph-supported gap fills from MUMmer,
  minimap2, GFA, GAF, and Hi-C-like evidence.
authors:
  - family-names: Roth
    given-names: Conrad
version: "0.2.28"
url: "https://github.com/rotheconrad/chromosort"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rotheconrad/chromosort"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - genome assembly
  - contig sorting
  - scaffolding
  - MUMmer
  - minimap2
  - GFA
  - bioinformatics
  - plant genomics
